<article class="env-definition" id="01LW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01LW">Definition <span data-tag="01LW">27.4.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebras. The <em>relative spectrum of $\mathcal{A}$ over $S$</em>, or simply the <em>spectrum of $\mathcal{A}$ over $S$</em> is the scheme constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/01LP" data-tag="01LP">27.3.4</a> which represents the functor $F$ (<a href="/tag/01LR" data-tag="01LR">27.4.0.1</a>), see Lemma <a href="/tag/01LV" data-tag="01LV">27.4.4</a>. We denote it $\pi : \underline{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}}_ S(\mathcal{A}) \to S$. The “universal family” is a morphism of $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebras </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{A} \longrightarrow \pi _*\mathcal{O}_{\underline{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}}_ S(\mathcal{A})}  \]
</div>
</article>